Step by Step Algorithm:

Step 1: Initialize three variables:
        le = 1 (left running product)
        ri = 1 (right running product)
        max = -∞ (to store maximum product)
Step 2: Get the length of the array n.
Step 3: Traverse the array from index 0 to n - 1.
Step 4: If le becomes 0, reset it to 1.
Step 5: If ri becomes 0, reset it to 1.
Step 6: Multiply:
        le = le * nums[i] (left to right)
        ri = ri * nums[n - i - 1] (right to left)
Step 7: Update maximum value:
        max = max(max, le, ri)
Step 8: Continue until all elements are processed.
Step 9: Return max.

Time Complexity: O(n)
Space Complexity: O(1)


----> Code <----

class Solution {
    public int maxProduct(int[] nums) {
        int le=1,ri=1,max=Integer.MIN_VALUE;
        int n=nums.length;
        for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
            if(le==0)le=1;
            if(ri==0)ri=1;
            le*=nums[i];
            ri*=nums[n-i-1];
            max=Math.max(max,Math.max(le,ri));
        }
        return max;
    }
}
